WEBVTT

00:00:55.704 --> 00:01:00.162
Neurons in the brain communicate 
at dedicated sites called “synapses”

00:01:00.204 --> 00:01:02.871
using specialized neurotransmitters.

00:01:02.912 --> 00:01:07.579
If two neurons communicate repeatedly,
a remarkable thing happens:

00:01:07.621 --> 00:01:11.163
the efficiency of communication
between them increases.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:14.371
This process, called 
“long term potentiation”,

00:01:14.413 --> 00:01:19.329
is considered to be a mechanism
by which memories are stored long-term,

00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:22.413
but how do some memories get lost?

00:01:22.621 --> 00:01:25.079
Age is one factor.

00:01:25.121 --> 00:01:28.204
As we get older, synapses 
begin to falter and weaken,

00:01:28.246 --> 00:01:31.204
affecting how easily
we can retrieve memories.